E2.evidence:
The abort is an invalid free inside the usb_cam process caused by usb_cam's own AVPacket memory handling in its MJPEG converter, introduced by usb_cam's own memory-leak work; it occurs with any MJPEG camera and any image consumer. Maintainer on the duplicate report #274: "Sorry this was a result of my latest work on trying to address some memory leaks" (https://github.com/ros-drivers/usb_cam/issues/274). Fix commits are framed as packet lifetime management inside usb_cam: "Only unref packet in destructor" (afa9dd6531f41cbb3f4c1eef5048be17b0f93972) and "Allocate unique avpacket for each frame" (bd6bb91c7279819ad4136001b5e5a138dffa5452), the latter replacing "av_packet_from_data(
      m_avpacket,
      const_cast<uint8_t *>(reinterpret_cast<const uint8_t *>(src)),
      bytes_used);" with "auto avpacket = av_packet_alloc();
    av_new_packet(avpacket, bytes_used);
    memcpy(avpacket->data, src, bytes_used);" (https://github.com/ros-drivers/usb_cam/pull/279).
